.docname {Naming Conventions}
.include {docs}

A name says what a thing is, so a reader can guess its role without opening it. Linters check the code style of each language; review checks everything else on this page.

---

## Services

A service has **one short name**, the same on every surface, with no `-service` suffix.

| Surface | Example |
|---|---|
| Directory | `backend/telemetry`, `backend/digital-twin` |
| Cargo crate, Go module, binary | `telemetry`, `digital-twin` |
| moon project | `telemetry`, `digital-twin` |
| Compose service, hostname | `telemetry:3000`, `digital-twin:3000` |
| Environment variable | `TELEMETRY_URL`, `DIGITAL_TWIN_URL` |
| Docker image | `crowdvision-telemetry` |
| Kubernetes manifest | `k8s/deployments/telemetry.yml` |
| Doc page | `documentation/docs/services/telemetry.qd` |

- Why: a suffix on some surfaces and not others is how a key in `.github/services.json` ends up disagreeing with a directory.
- `claims-gateway` and `provisioner` are named for what they are, a gateway and a reconciler.

**Known exceptions**

| Name | Where | Short form used |
|---|---|---|
| `digital-twin` | `.github/services.json` key, Docker image, commit scope | `twin`, `crowdvision-twin` |
| `sensor-simulator` | Docker image | `crowdvision-simulator` |
| `claims-gateway` | commit scope | `gateway` |

---

## Top-level folders

The folder says what kind of thing it holds.

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `backend/<name>/` | A deployable service |
| `backend/libs/` | Go modules built into services, never deployed |
| `backend/acceptance/` | The cross-service acceptance suite. Each service keeps its own `tests/` |
| `schemas/` | Every shape that crosses a service boundary: `json/` schemas, `fixtures/`, Rust crates `*-schema` |
| `simulators/` | Fake sensors and routers for local runs |
| `tooling/` | Shared tool config, like `eslint-config` |

---

## Rust

The six Rust services and the four `*-schema` crates follow standard Rust style, checked by `clippy`.

| Thing | Style | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Module, file | `snake_case` | `redis_fanout.rs`, `alert_listener.rs` |
| Function | `snake_case` | `filtered_channel`, `resolve_channel` |
| Type, trait | `PascalCase` | `TelemetryEnvelope`, `AlertEvent` |
| Constant | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `RAW_CHANNEL`, `ALERTS_TOPIC` |
| Schema crate | `<area>-schema`, used as `<area>_schema` | `telemetry-schema`, `telemetry_schema::AlertEvent` |

Folder names inside a service follow its layering:

| Service | Folders |
|---|---|
| `telemetry` | `types/`, `kernel/`, `plugins/`, `adapters/` |
| `digital-twin`, `notification`, `chat` | `domain/`, `service/`, `adapters/driving/`, `adapters/driven/` |
| `socket` | `core/`, `shell/` |
| `dashboard` | flat: `api/`, `infra/`, `tunnel.rs` |

---

## Go

`claims-gateway`, `tenancy`, `registry`, `provisioner` and the three `backend/libs/` modules follow standard Go style, checked by `gofmt` and `go vet`.

| Thing | Style | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Package, folder | one lowercase word, no underscores | `tenancyclient`, `storefake`, `oidcverifier` |
| Exported name | `PascalCase` | `RequireSignature`, `Config` |
| Unexported name | `camelCase` | `roleIn`, `handler` |
| Constant | `PascalCase` or `camelCase`, by visibility | never `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` |

Layout:

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `cmd/<svc>/main.go` | Wiring only |
| `internal/api` | HTTP handlers |
| `internal/service` | The rules |
| `internal/store`, `internal/storefake` | Postgres, and its in-memory stand-in for tests |
| `internal/<other>client` | A client for another service, like `tenancyclient` |
| `internal/config` | Environment variables |

---

## Python

`agent`, `aq-simulator`, `ap-simulator` and `backend/acceptance` follow PEP 8, checked by `ruff`.

| Thing | Style | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Module, function, variable | `snake_case` | `cedar_authz.py`, `can_ingest_documents` |
| Class | `PascalCase` | `AuthUser` |
| Constant | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `ROLE_WEIGHTS` |
| Agent tool name | `snake_case`, verb first | `search_docs`, `get_latest_sensor_data` |

---

## TypeScript

### Frontend, Vue 3

| Thing | Style | Example | Avoid |
|---|---|---|---|
| Component | `PascalCase`, two words or more | `ChatBubble.vue`, `NotificationMenu.vue` | `card.vue` |
| Component folder | feature, then role | `components/commons/forms/TextInput.vue` | |
| View, a page with a route | `PascalCase` + `View` | `DashboardView.vue`, `DomainsView.vue` | `Dashboard.vue` |
| Folder under `views/`, `components/`, `composables/`, `utils/`, `stores/`, `types/` | `kebab-case`, one per feature | `digital-twin/`, `administration/` | grouping by widget kind, like `modals/` |
| Shared pieces | `commons/` inside each of those folders | `composables/commons/useApi.ts` | |
| Composable | `camelCase`, starts with `use` | `useAuth.ts`, `useSessionKeepAlive.ts` | `getAuth.ts` |
| Pinia store | file `camelCase`, export `use<Name>Store` | `stores/digital-twin/buildings.ts`, `useBuildingsStore` | |
| Helper | `camelCase` | `utils/commons/telemetry.ts` | `Telemetry.ts` |
| Unit test | beside the file, `.spec.ts` | `telemetry.spec.ts` | |

### `sensor-simulator`, Node

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `src/index.ts` | Start-up |
| `src/router.ts` | Routes |
| `src/controller/` | HTTP handlers, like `simController.ts` |
| `src/services/` | The simulation, like `simulatorService.ts` |
| `src/models/` | Shapes, like `signal.ts` |

---

## Messages

| Thing | Style | Example | Rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| Kafka topic | `kebab-case`, what happened | `building-registration-requested`, `alerts` | Declared once, in a `schemas/*-schema` crate |
| Dead-letter topic | topic + `.dlq` | `alerts.dlq` | |
| Kafka consumer group | what it reads, not who reads | `alerts`, `building-registrations`, `wifi-observations` | See "Renaming carries data" |
| Redis channel | `area:kind[:id]` | `telemetry:raw`, `telemetry:filtered:b1` | Built only by `*-schema` functions |
| Socket.IO room | `building:<id>`, `domain:<name>` | `building:b1` | Built only in `socket/src/core/rooms.rs` |
| Cedar action | `PascalCase` verb | `Read`, `Edit`, `IngestDocuments` | Declared in `backend/libs/auth-policy` |
| System identity | `system:<name>` | `system:notification-service` | Never renamed: pinned by a test |

---

## Branches

`<type>/<short-kebab-description>`, using the commit types.

| Type | Example |
|---|---|
| `feat` | `feat/private-domains` |
| `fix` | `fix/jwt-expiry-off-by-one` |
| `chore` | `chore/bump-dependencies` |
| `docs` | `docs/reshaping` |
| `refactor` | `refactor/extract-token-service` |

---

## Commit scopes

The scope is the service or area, so history can be filtered by part:

`gateway`, `tenancy`, `registry`, `provisioner`, `twin`, `telemetry`, `dashboard`, `notification`, `socket`, `chat`, `frontend`, `agent`, `ci`, `docs`, `k8s`.

```text
feat(twin): add per-room colour overrides
fix(gateway): reject expired refresh tokens
```

Nothing in CI checks the format. A malformed message is silently treated as "no release": [Release Please](release-please.qd).

---

## Other names

| Thing | Style | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Environment variable | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `GATEWAY_ISSUER`, `INTERNAL_SIGNING_SECRET` |
| Variable naming another service | `<SERVICE>_URL` | `TELEMETRY_URL` |
| Metric source for `dashboard` | anything ending in `_METRICS_URL` | `SENSOR_METRICS_URL`, `TWIN_METRICS_URL` |
| Workflow file | `<kind>-<name>.yml`, kind is `ci`, `cd`, `maint` or `tpl` | `ci-gate.yml`, `cd-release.yml`, `tpl-rust-ci.yml` |
| Doc page | `kebab-case.qd` | `naming-conventions.qd` |
| Fixture, JSON schema | `kebab-case.json`, `kebab-case.schema.json` | `telemetry-envelope.json` |

---

## Renaming carries data

Some names own stored state. Changing one starts from empty, with no error.

| Name | What a rename does |
|---|---|
| Compose volume | Compose builds the real name from the project and the declared name. A new name mounts a **new, empty** volume and leaves the old one with all the data. Move the data in the same change |
| Kafka consumer group | A group with no saved position starts from the oldest message: the whole topic is read again. Harmless for registrations. For `alerts` it sends old breaches again, only held back by the 5-minute cooldown |
| Database name | A rename is a migration, so names stay: `chatdb`, `twindb`, `notificationdb` |
| System identity | `system:notification-service` keeps its old name: a test pins it byte for byte, and logs keep one stable source |

.box {`dashboard` ignores the database in its URI} type:{warning}
    Its compose `MONGO_URI` ends in `/contractsdb`, but `infra/db.rs` always opens database `crowdvision`, collection `preferences`. The path in the URI changes nothing.

.box {Check for orphans after a rename} type:{warning}
    `docker volume ls` lists every volume. One no compose file names is orphaned: move its data or delete it on purpose.
